{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_migration_toolkit", "label": "Schema-evolution toolkit", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Event-sourced systems keep events forever, so a v1 event stays in the journal when v3 ships. Five cooperating tools answer how to evolve event/state shapes without breaking recovery: the envelope, the schema registry, defaultsAdapter, migratingAdapter and WrapLegacy.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_strategy_decision_tree", "label": "Picking a migration strategy", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Additive change goes to defaultsAdapter; transformable old-to-new goes to migratingAdapter (single- or multi-step); anything else \u2014 renames, splits, joins \u2014 to a custom EventAdapter.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_stateadapter", "label": "StateAdapter", "file_type": "document", "rationale": "DurableStateActor has the same machinery via stateAdapter(); persisted states are wrapped in the same _v/_t/_e envelope, so the same migration tools work for either kind of persistence.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_operational_rollout_phases", "label": "Operational rollout phases", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Deploy the adapter able to read old and new, verify by recovering several persistenceIds, start writing the new shape, and only once snapshots cover the old events consider simplifying the chain.", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_strategy_decision_tree", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_migration_toolkit", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_operational_rollout_phases", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_migration_toolkit", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_migration_toolkit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_envelope_format_versioned_envelope", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_migration_toolkit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_default_adapter_defaultsadapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/migration/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_overview_migration_toolkit", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_migration_migrating_adapter_migratingadapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs